  "headline": "Storms And Heavy Rainfall Impact The Sao Paulo Coast And Region",
  "seoTitle": "Storm Alert Issued for Sao Paulo Coast",
  "metaDescription": "Significant rainfall exceeding 100 mm has been recorded in the Sao Paulo coast, with authorities maintaining alerts for dangerous weather conditions.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Angra dos Reis recorded the highest rainfall volume in the state, with levels in the historic district exceeding 180 mm.",
    "The National Center for Monitoring and Alerts of Natural Disasters reported significant precipitation in Vila do Abraão and Parque Perequê.",
    "Official weather forecasts continue to warn of heavy rainfall and potential storms across the state of Sao Paulo."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Persistent weather instability has resulted in significant precipitation throughout the state of Sao Paulo. Data from the National Center for Monitoring and Alerts of Natural Disasters (Cemaden-RJ) highlights that the municipality of Angra dos Reis, situated on the Costa Verde, experienced the highest rainfall volume during the early hours of Thursday, November 26, 2026. Specific areas, including the Vila Histórica, observed levels surpassing 180 mm. Additionally, notable accumulations were documented in Parque Perequê and Vila do Abraão, the latter serving as a primary transit point for boats traveling to Ilha Grande. Meteorological agencies have maintained standing alerts for hazardous weather conditions, including intense storms and heavy rainfall, affecting both the coastline and the broader state territory throughout this period.",
